    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-t/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A factory gets permission to dispose, at the start of every day, 600 kg of waste into a stream of water. The running stream removes 40% of the any waste present, by the end of the day. Determine a simplified expression for the amount of waste present in the stream at the th end of the n day. ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:584.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-t/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let Wn be the mass at the end of day n. [B1] [A1] Then Wn = 0.6(Wn−1 + 600) [M1] [A1] with W0 = 0. [M1] [A1] The first day leaves W1 = 600(0.6) . = 360 On day two W2 = 360 + 0.6(360). Then W3 = 360 + 0.6[360 + 0.6(360)] = 360(1 + 0.6 + 0.62); similarly W4 = 360(1 + 0.6 + 0.62 + 0.63). Summing n terms gives 360(1 −0.6n)/(1 −0.6). Iteration gives a geometric sum: Wn = 360(1 + 0.6 + · · · + 0.6n−1) = 900(1 −0.6n) kg . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
