      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-t/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) Since y = ln 2/ ln x, the domain is x &gt; 0, x̸ = 1. The curve decreases on each interval, has a vertical asymptote x = 1, [B1] and approaches 0 from below as x →0+ and from above as x →∞. [A1] (b) P = (2, 1). [B1] [A1] Differentiate y = (ln 2)(ln x)−1 to obtain dy/dx = −(ln 2)(ln x)−2/x.\" style=\"--madas-width:660.0px\"></figure>",
